# VibeTest — Angular 22 SPA/PWA

Offline-first course PWA. Spec: `docs/SPECIFICATION.md`. Tasks: `docs/tasks/`.

## Architecture & generation

- **Standalone only** — no NgModules
- **CLI** — Angular artifacts with a schematic: component, service, guard, pipe (interface via `ng g` when convenient)
- **Manual** — domain models, validators, Web Workers, pure functions, adapters, constants
- **Domain folders** (vertical slices; UI / application / infrastructure as needed — **do not pre-create layers**: add a subfolder only when an area has several files of the same role):
  - `courses/`, `player/`, `progress/`, `execution/`, `storage/`, `shared/ui/`
- Domain behavior — **pure functions** or domain types; **services** — DI, orchestration, side-effects (storage, Workers, HTTP later). One component, one responsibility; avoid injectable “service soup”
- **Smart / dumb** (guideline): pages and orchestration own data and state; reusable UI via `input()` / `output()`. Smart widgets with local UI logic are fine; do not pull HTTP/storage into `shared/ui` without a clear reason

## Code style

- TypeScript strict; `any` only at untyped external API boundaries; otherwise `unknown` + runtime checks
- `signal()` / `computed()`, `inject()`; control flow `@if`, `@for`, `@switch`
- Observables: `async` pipe or `toSignal()` as appropriate
- Reactive forms for non-trivial input
- SCSS, BEM-like classes, no inline styles in templates
- Do not edit `angular.json` / `tsconfig*.json` without need

## PWA

- Service Worker in production build (`ng build`), not by default in `ng serve`; updates via `SwUpdate`

## Tests

```bash
ng test
```

- Required for: domain logic, storage, guards, pipes, non-trivial component logic
- Tests assert **behavior**, not implementation details
- Config, types, simple markup — no mandatory test-first
- Before finishing a task: `ng test` green (when tests are set up)
- `*.spec.ts` next to source

## Tasks & git

Tasks under `docs/tasks/` are agent context. **Task status = folder** (`backlog` → `in-progress` → `done`); do not duplicate status in `REPORT.md`.

- `backlog/vt-{n}-{slug}.md` — plan
- `in-progress/vt-{n}-{slug}/` — `TASK.md` + `REPORT.md` (`branch:` in REPORT frontmatter)
- `done/vt-{n}-{slug}/` — after merge to `main`
- `archive/{YYYY-MM}/` — move old `done` **in batches**, only on request
- Templates: `_template/backlog-task.md`, `REPORT.md`
- `{n}`: max among all `vt-*` + 1; slug — kebab-case

**Commits** — WIP commits on `feature/vt-{n}-{slug}` are free and need no confirmation (they get squashed away). Never commit directly to `main`.

**Merge** — only after explicit request (“merge vt-{n}”, “merge to main”): **rebase + squash**, one commit per task, linear `main`. The request also authorizes the doc move, the squash commit and pushing `main`:

1. Last branch commit: `in-progress/vt-{n}-{slug}/` → `done/vt-{n}-{slug}/` + final `REPORT.md`
2. `git rebase main` — resolve conflicts on the branch, never in `main`
3. Squash the branch into one commit (`git reset --soft main && git commit`); message `vt-{n}: {short summary}` — show it before committing
4. `git switch main && git merge --ff-only feature/vt-{n}-{slug}`, push, delete the branch

No merge commits; merged state must not land in `main` while the task folder is still under `in-progress/`.

**Working on vt-{n}:** branch `feature/vt-{n}-{slug}` from `main`; move backlog → `in-progress/` + `REPORT.md`; read `TASK.md` and spec; update `REPORT.md`; one task — one branch. Ready for review: filled `REPORT.md`, green tests; user reviews `main..feature/...`.

## Never

- Direct commits to `main`
- Merge commits in `main` (history stays linear)
- Duplicate logic across domain areas
- Secrets, `.env`, `node_modules/` in git
